WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.293
- Usually I do
the introductions, but I—

00:00:02.293 --> 00:00:03.920
This is you.
This is your guy.

00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:05.255
- This is my guy.

00:00:05.255 --> 00:00:08.800
I mean, this is
the original CJ2K.

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:10.260
My man right here.

00:00:10.260 --> 00:00:12.095
I didn't know what to expect
when I saw

00:00:12.095 --> 00:00:13.638
this guy in person as a player.
Like—

00:00:13.638 --> 00:00:15.015
- Cuz he was a rookie
when you were there.

00:00:15.015 --> 00:00:16.808
- He was a rookie.

00:00:16.808 --> 00:00:18.893
And in training camp, I was
with the Tampa Bay Buccaneers.

00:00:18.893 --> 00:00:21.396
So I—
that team, as he'll tell you

00:00:21.396 --> 00:00:23.690
had a bunch of Texas guys
on the Tennessee Titans team.

00:00:23.690 --> 00:00:25.775
And they kept telling me,
"Man, this Chris Johnson

00:00:25.775 --> 00:00:27.027
is a baller, man.

00:00:27.027 --> 00:00:28.611
We've never seen
anybody so fast."

00:00:28.611 --> 00:00:30.739
And I was like,
"Yeah, bleh, bleh, bleh, bleh."

00:00:30.739 --> 00:00:33.700
But then I got there and

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:36.995
yes, one of the most special
talents I have ever been around.

00:00:36.995 --> 00:00:39.080
- And then, your memories
of Chris Simms back then?

00:00:39.080 --> 00:00:42.042
- Oh, man. He used to talk trash
to me before every game.

00:00:42.042 --> 00:00:43.752
- Stop.
- I think it was probably

00:00:43.752 --> 00:00:44.961
like Week 2 or Week 3.

00:00:44.961 --> 00:00:46.588
He was like, "Ah, come on"

00:00:46.588 --> 00:00:49.257
I was—I think I had went
for 100 yards, like, twice.

00:00:49.257 --> 00:00:50.759
He's like, "Come on, man.

00:00:50.759 --> 00:00:53.053
I'm tired of seeing these 10-,
15-yard runs.

00:00:53.053 --> 00:00:54.512
Break off somethin' long."

00:00:54.512 --> 00:00:57.140
I think, that same game,
LenDale broke for 80

00:00:57.140 --> 00:00:59.392
and I came right back
and broke for, like, 76.

00:00:59.392 --> 00:01:00.810
- Kansas City.
- Kansas City.

00:01:00.810 --> 00:01:02.604
- Kansas City game.
He did.

00:01:02.604 --> 00:01:04.898
- I feel like that's when the
Smash and Dash thing took off.

00:01:04.898 --> 00:01:06.191
- Right. It did.

00:01:06.191 --> 00:01:07.484
- When those two big
runs happened.

00:01:07.484 --> 00:01:08.985
- Yeah.
- Yep.

00:01:08.985 --> 00:01:10.820
- I think that's
a nickname that I feel like

00:01:10.820 --> 00:01:13.031
they try to give
to a lot of duos now.

00:01:13.031 --> 00:01:14.449
But you guys
were Smash and Dash.

00:01:14.449 --> 00:01:15.867
- Yeah, yeah, we started that.

00:01:15.867 --> 00:01:18.036
They asked us, like,
what was our name.

00:01:18.036 --> 00:01:19.621
-Yes.

00:01:19.621 --> 00:01:21.164
- And LenDale was like,
"We Smash and Dash."

00:01:21.164 --> 00:01:22.624
- Right.
- He came up with Smash and Dash

00:01:22.624 --> 00:01:24.042
and then ever since then

00:01:24.042 --> 00:01:26.044
they just started
calling us that every week.

00:01:26.044 --> 00:01:27.504
- Smash and Dash, OK

00:01:27.504 --> 00:01:29.756
him and LenDale,
I mean, characters

00:01:29.756 --> 00:01:31.674
and LenDale
especially a character.

00:01:31.674 --> 00:01:33.927
- That's an all-time
running back room.

00:01:33.927 --> 00:01:35.095
- Yeah.
- Yes.

00:01:35.095 --> 00:01:37.097
And LenDale—

00:01:37.097 --> 00:01:40.100
we can put him on blast now
cuz his career is over—

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:43.103
- [Laughing]
- He was late a lot, OK?

00:01:43.103 --> 00:01:45.396
I mean, late a lot.
- Right.

00:01:45.396 --> 00:01:48.274
- Like, and always had
a different excuse.

00:01:48.274 --> 00:01:50.026
Creative as hell, right?

00:01:50.026 --> 00:01:52.070
- How much is "late"?
- Yeah, see? He knows it's true.

00:01:52.070 --> 00:01:54.280
Like, if we had an 8:30 meeting

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:57.492
LenDale was, I felt like,
never there at 8:30.

00:01:57.492 --> 00:01:59.452
Never.
- And this is every day?

00:01:59.452 --> 00:02:00.954
- I mean, at least once
or twice a week.

00:02:00.954 --> 00:02:02.288
- OK.

00:02:02.288 --> 00:02:04.666
- And he'd always have
some great excuse.

00:02:04.666 --> 00:02:06.084
I mean, great.

00:02:06.084 --> 00:02:07.627
What do you think
his best excuse was?

00:02:07.627 --> 00:02:09.921
What was one you remember,
you remember any good ones?

00:02:09.921 --> 00:02:13.925
- Yeah. He was late one time,
and he came in and he was like

00:02:13.925 --> 00:02:17.929
"Man, I had to pull over
to the gas station bathroom

00:02:17.929 --> 00:02:19.430
and my stomach was hurting.

00:02:19.430 --> 00:02:21.432
I had to use the bathroom."
- He was just—

00:02:21.432 --> 00:02:24.102
So his excuse was "I took a crap
at a gas station."

00:02:24.102 --> 00:02:26.104
- I had to take a crap
in a bathroom, yes.

00:02:26.104 --> 00:02:29.065
- And then when he says that,
the team explodes?

00:02:29.065 --> 00:02:31.734
- No, actually.
Cuz it's a serious setting.

00:02:31.734 --> 00:02:33.278
- [Laughing]
- I mean, we're all shaking
our head like

00:02:33.278 --> 00:02:34.821
"What a bunch of bullcrap
that is."

00:02:34.821 --> 00:02:36.281
But there's nothin' we can say

00:02:36.281 --> 00:02:37.782
cuz Jeff Fisher is still
the head coach

00:02:37.782 --> 00:02:39.284
and he's standing
in front of the room

00:02:39.284 --> 00:02:40.410
and we're not gonna butt
into that conversation.

00:02:40.410 --> 00:02:40.869
and we're not gonna butt
into that conversation.

